# Rust
target/
**/target/
Cargo.lock.bak
*.pdb

# Spike artifacts
mutants.out/
**/mutants.out/
# 453 files of this were committed by accident in fd2ff5d and churned in every
# `git status` afterwards -- which is how `git add -A` came to sweep up things
# nobody meant to commit.
mutants.out.old/
**/mutants.out.old/
spikes/**/out/
spikes/results/*.json

# Python bytecode caches. `brand/final/` carries the logo-tracing scripts, and
# one compiled `.pyc` was committed with them -- machine-specific, regenerated
# on every run, and it still named the project by its old name months later.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Fuzzing corpora and crash artifacts. The corpus is machine-generated and
# grows without bound; a crashing input, if one is ever found, gets committed
# deliberately as a regression test rather than swept in by a glob.
fuzz/target/
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/

# Node dependency trees. `site/` carries one, and `git add -A` staged 5,000+
# files from it once before this line existed. Machine-generated, restorable
# from a lockfile, and large enough to bury a real diff.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Commit-message scratch. Written, used with `git commit -F`, deleted -- and
# staged by `git add -A` three times before this line existed.
msg.txt
m.txt
.native/

# Staged by apps/desktop/src-tauri/build.rs from the workspace target dir, so
# that `bundle.resources` has a stable relative path to declare. Build output,
# never source.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/engines/

# The built site. `site/scripts/gates.mjs` reads `site/dist/`, so a committed
# copy goes stale the moment a page changes and the gates then report failures
# about markup nobody wrote -- twice, in one session, costing a diagnosis each
# time. It is regenerated by `npm run build --prefix site` in one step.
site/dist/
# Astro's incremental cache. Machine-generated, per-machine, and it churns on
# every build.
site/.astro/

# Packaged installers. `tauri build` drops one at the repo root; it is 15 MB of
# output rebuildable from source, and a binary in git history cannot be removed
# from it later.
/OpenConvert_*.exe
*.msi
*.AppImage
*.dmg

# Personal test material. Real recordings and their transcripts, kept beside
# the repo for convenience and belonging to whoever made them -- not fixtures,
# not licensed for redistribution, and 18 MB.
Samples/

# Vercel's deploy state. `site/.vercel/` holds the project linkage and a build
# cache: machine-specific, regenerated by `vercel link`, and it carries the
# project and org ids, which are not worth putting in history.
site/.vercel/

# Secrets. The contact form reads RESEND_API_KEY from the environment; a key
# committed is a key revoked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Private development records. These stay available in the local checkout but
# are deliberately excluded from the public repository and release archives.
/.claude/
/agent-briefs/
/spikes/
/docs/plans/
/docs/process/
/docs/TODO.md
/docs/IMPROVEMENTS.md
/docs/todo-*.md
/docs/workspace-improvements.md
**/HANDOFF.md
/docs/reviews/

# Exploratory brand work is private; only the selected assets under
# brand/final and brand/logo belong in the public source tree.
/brand/animal-concepts/
/brand/route-variants/
/brand/previews/
/brand/aioc-*
/brand/concept-*
/brand/README.md

# Screenshot source captures and conversion receipts can contain local working
# context. The optimized, reviewed images in site/public/shots remain public.
/site/tools/shots/raw/
/site/tools/shots/receipts/
